From: xnulinux
Subject: [PATCH] linux64: a halt or restart ends the run in the host

Hosted, there is no machine to halt or reset: halt_all_cpus found no platform handler and span with interrupts masked,
holding its Linux CPU for good (and the others where they were). The host is told instead (LINUX64_CALL_HALT) and ends
the run on every CPU.
---
diff --git a/osfmk/arm64/machine_routines.c b/osfmk/arm64/machine_routines.c
--- a/osfmk/arm64/machine_routines.c
+++ b/osfmk/arm64/machine_routines.c
@@ -941,6 +941,13 @@
 __attribute__((noreturn))
 void
 halt_all_cpus(boolean_t reboot)
 {
+	{
+		/* LINUX64 (xnulinux): no machine to halt or reset; the host ends the run (the call does not return). */
+		if (linux64_hook) {
+			printf(reboot ? "MACH Reboot\n" : "CPU halted\n");
+			linux64_call2(LINUX64_CALL_HALT, reboot ? 1 : 0, 0);
+		}
+	}
 	if (reboot) {
 		printf("MACH Reboot\n");
